# 🚦 Chennai Traffic Predictor

## 📌 Project Overview

The **Chennai Traffic Predictor** is a machine learning–based system designed to predict traffic congestion levels on major roads in Chennai. It analyzes historical traffic data along with time, location, and environmental factors to provide accurate traffic predictions.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

* Predict traffic congestion levels in Chennai.
* Help commuters plan better travel routes.
* Assist traffic authorities in effective traffic management.
* Support smart-city transportation systems.

---

## 🧠 Technologies Used

| Technology               | Purpose                    |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------- |
| **Programming Language** | Python                     |
| **Machine Learning**     | Scikit-learn / XGBoost     |
| **Data Handling**        | Pandas, NumPy              |
| **Visualization**        | Matplotlib / Seaborn       |
| **Frontend (Optional)**  | HTML, CSS, JavaScript      |
| **Backend (Optional)**   | Flask / Django             |
| **Deployment**           | Localhost / Cloud Platform |

---

## 📊 Features

* Time-based traffic prediction (peak & non-peak hours).
* Location-based congestion analysis.
* Real-time and historical data support.
* Predicts traffic as **Low, Medium, or High**.
* Explainable and interpretable results.

---

## 🏗️ System Architecture

The system follows these major stages:

```text
Data Collection
       ↓
Data Preprocessing
       ↓
Feature Engineering
       ↓
Model Training
       ↓
Traffic Prediction
       ↓
Result Visualization
```

---

## ▶️ How to Run the Project

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vdennyrichard-gif/Chennai-Traffic-Predictor.git
```

### 2. Open the project directory

```bash
cd Chennai-Traffic-Predictor
```

### 3. Install required libraries

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Run the application

```bash
python app.py
```

---

## 📈 Output

The project provides:

* Traffic congestion prediction for selected routes.
* Visual graphs showing traffic trends.
* Clear classification of congestion levels.

